# Author: Oleksii Hnidan
# Project: web-security26 | Lab: 5 | File: multi-user-basic.http

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tracks

### 1. Admin may use the admin route - 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/admin
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Accept: application/json

### 2. User may not use the admin route - 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/admin
Authorization: Basic user user
Accept: application/json

### 3. User may use the user route - 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/user
Authorization: Basic user user
Accept: application/json

### 4. Admin may not use the user-only route - 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/user
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Accept: application/json

### 5. Admin is a catalog member - 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/member
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Accept: application/json

### 6. User is a catalog member - 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/member
Authorization: Basic user user
Accept: application/json

### 7. Superadmin may use the superadmin route - 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/superadmin
Authorization: Basic superadmin superadmin
Accept: application/json

### 8. Admin may not use the superadmin route - 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/superadmin
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Accept: application/json

### 9. Any authenticated user may list tracks - 200
GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Basic superadmin superadmin
Accept: application/json

### 10. An anonymous user may not list tracks - 401
GET {{baseUrl}}
Accept: application/json
